// "[subject] gains N life" ([CR#119.3]) — the third-person life-gain verb
// phrase. A parse/render template over the core `ChangeLife` verb for the
// declarative-subject production ("Each player gains 2 life", "Target player
// gains 3 life"); expands in place to `ChangeLife(who, Up(n))`.
//
// `who` (Param(0)) is a REAL slot, not a coordinate scraped off a wrapper.
// Before the action role reshape this macro took only the count, and the
// acting player was supplied by an enclosing `By(It, …)` that the migrations
// declarative-subject parser spliced in. `By` is gone — role slots are never
// defaulted now — so the subject rides the macro's own leading `${0}` exactly
// as `Draws`/`Mills` already did, and the parser matches this template
// against "it gains N life" instead of wrapping the result.
//
// Usage: GainsLife(It, 2) (the Each-bound / announced player subject) /
// GainsLife(Target(0), 3).
(
    name: "GainsLife",
    template: "${0} gains ${1} life",
    kinds: [Action],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    body: ChangeLife(Param(0), Up(Param(1))),
)
